    "title": "pandas.DatetimeTZDtype — pandas 2.1.4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DatetimeTZDtype#\n\n- \n*class* pandas.DatetimeTZDtype(*unit='ns'* ,*tz=None* )[source]#\n- An ExtensionDtype for timezone-aware datetime data. **This is not an actual numpy dtype** , but a duck type.\n  - Parameters:\n    - **unit** str, default “ns”\n    - The precision of the datetime data. Currently limited to `\"ns\"` .\n    - **tz** str, int, or datetime.tzinfo\n    - The timezone.\n  - Raises:\n    - ZoneInfoNotFoundError\n    - When the requested timezone cannot be found.\n Examples >>> from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo >>> pd.DatetimeTZDtype(tz=ZoneInfo('UTC')) datetime64[ns, UTC] >>> pd.DatetimeTZDtype(tz=ZoneInfo('Europe/Paris')) datetime64[ns, Europe/Paris] Attributes `unit`The precision of the datetime data. `tz`The timezone. Methods **None**",
